---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL, PRODUCT_NAME } from "../consts";

const title = "Data & privacy";
const description =
  "How OpenGolfLab handles your data: the app is local-first, contribution is opt-in and anonymized, only aggregates are published, your raw shots are never sold, and this website measures traffic without cookies.";
const updated = "July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="section-tight priv-hero">
    <div class="container priv-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
      <h1>Data &amp; privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:0.9rem;">
        {PRODUCT_NAME} is local-first: your shots stay on your machine. Sharing
        data with the community is entirely opt-in, always anonymized, and only
        ever published as combined averages, never your raw shots, never sold.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container priv-body">
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The app is local-first</h2>
      <p>
        {PRODUCT_NAME} runs entirely on your Windows PC. Your shot history lives
        in local files next to the app, there's no account to create, and
        nothing is uploaded anywhere as part of normal use. If you never opt in
        to contribute, no data ever leaves your machine.
      </p>

      <h2>This website counts visits, without cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The website is separate from the app, and it does measure traffic. It
        uses <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/"
          rel="noopener nofollow">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
        >, which is cookieless: it sets no cookie, stores nothing on your
        device, and assigns you no identifier that follows you between pages,
        sites or visits. That's why you have never seen a cookie banner here.
        What it records is the page, the referring site, and coarse
        browser/country/device information, in aggregate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside it, a handful of first-party counters record which parts of
        the site actually work: a download button being clicked, a calculator
        being run, a section being read. They post to opengolflab.com itself,
        no third party is involved, and each one carries the event name and the
        page it happened on and nothing else, no identifier, no session, no
        profile. Their entire purpose is telling whether people find the
        contribute pitch, which is the thing this project is currently stuck
        on. They respect
        <a
          href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/API/Navigator/doNotTrack"
          rel="noopener nofollow">Do Not Track</a
        >: turn it on and nothing is sent.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is all entirely separate from {PRODUCT_NAME} itself. It runs on
        this website only, it never runs in the app, it can't see your shot
        data, and it isn't connected to contributions in any way. The previous
        version of this site used Google Analytics; it was removed, because a
        local-first project has no business shipping a third-party cookie tag.
      </p>

      <h2>Contributing is opt-in</h2>
      <p>
        Sharing data with OpenGolfLab is off by default. It only happens when
        you explicitly turn on the opt-in inside the app and export a
        contribution. You can turn it off again at any time, and you choose when
        (and whether) to submit anything.
      </p>

      <h2>What a contribution includes</h2>
      <p>
        When you opt in, the app builds an anonymized bundle of shot metrics:
        club, ball and club speed, launch angle, spin, carry, and similar
        per-shot numbers, plus an optional handicap <em>band</em> (a range like
        “10–14”, never an exact index) and, if you enter them, the ball or club
        model. Every value is a measurement of a golf shot.
      </p>

      <h2>What it never includes</h2>
      <p>
        Contributions never contain your name, email, file paths, device
        identifiers, or precise timestamps. There's no account and nothing
        tying a bundle back to you or to your visits to this website, a random,
        non-identifying id is used only to avoid counting the same submission
        twice.
      </p>

      <h2>How contributed data is used</h2>
      <p>
        Raw submissions are kept private. Only <strong>combined community
        aggregates</strong>, distributions, per-club averages and ranges, ball
        comparisons, are ever published on this site. Individual raw shots are
        not published and are not sold to anyone, including equipment brands.
        The aggregates exist to help golfers make better-informed gear
        decisions, and that's it.
      </p>

      <h2>Open by design</h2>
      <p>
        The exact list of fields a contribution contains, and the code that
        aggregates the data, are developed in the open on
        <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>,
        so anyone can see exactly what's collected and how it's summarized. The
        anonymization happens in the app, before anything is shared.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If how contributions are handled ever changes, the opt-in consent screen
        in the app and this page will be updated to match, and the change will
        apply going forward. Questions or concerns are welcome via the
        <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="priv-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .priv-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .priv-hero-inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 60ch;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .priv-body {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .priv-updated {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
